{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning workflow launch with file validation**\n\n**Reviewing model pinning before launch**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a912f7087d2ab8c79189cf052bf\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning workflow launch with file validation**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Reviewing model pinning before launch**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Architecture: use one bounded `goal` run (implement → inspect policy/schema → validate SQLite migration/idempotency → report). The graph is acyclic; deterministic checks cover transaction, row/order counts, dirty-email cleanup, constraints, rollback shape, and second-run safety. The run will edit only the requested SQL migration and create the four requested artifacts; it will not touch `schema.sql` or `migration_policy.md`. Stop when checks pass, otherwise repair within the bounded run.\n\nStage | Model | Thinking | Role  \nImplement/review | workflow default | high | migration design and contract review  \nValidation | deterministic tools | — | SQLite execution and assertions  \nFinal report | workflow default | medium | concise evidence summary\n\nI’m launching the single tracked implementation run now.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a94489487d2bcb98368b7dce38a\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3brtcWvViVpRIEUzXha3tpMv|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a97019c87d2b7d1354851a5e398","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"run","workflow":"goal","inputs":{"objective":"<keepContext>Safely repair the SQLite migration task using the exact files and requirements in the user request. Read the migration_policy.md before editing. Work directly on the absolute target paths supplied by the user. Edit only migration.sql among existing files; do not modify schema.sql or migration_policy.md. Create preflight_report.md, rollback.sql, postcheck.sql, and migration_report.md as explicitly requested. Preserve all users, orders, user_id references, and historical created_at values. Add non-null status default active; enforce unique non-null emails for future writes; clean exactly u4 -> ada+u4@example.com, u5 -> missing+u5@example.invalid, u6 -> missing+u6@example.invalid. Use an explicit SQLite transaction and make migration reruns safe and non-corrupting. Validate offline by executing against a copy of the schema/data, run migration twice, run postchecks, and test rollback after migration. The rollback must restore users to old columns id,email,name,created_at while preserving data. Do not use external services.</keepContext>","acceptance_criteria":"<keepContext>All requested files exist at the exact absolute paths. migration.sql is policy-compliant, transactional, idempotent, preserves every user/order and order.user_id, retains created_at, adds status NOT NULL DEFAULT active, and enforces email uniqueness/non-null for future writes while deterministically cleaning the three dirty users. preflight_report.md documents duplicate/null/blank issues and explicitly mentions dependent orders for u4, u5, u6. rollback.sql executes after migration and restores old users schema shape with preserved data. postcheck.sql contains executable checks for row counts, dependent orders, cleaned emails, and email/status constraints. migration_report.md covers strategy, cleanup, idempotency, rollback behavior/limitation, and postcheck use. SQLite execution, second migration run, and rollback tests pass without edits to forbidden files.</keepContext>","max_turns":4},"budget":{"maxDurationMs":300000,"warnAtPercent":80}}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2321,"output":753,"cacheRead":13824,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":153,"totalTokens":16898,"cost":{"input":0.00046420000000000