deterministic migrated email values, and document the cleanup.\n- Also create `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/049-043-db-migration-safety-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-020905-9b40d74d/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md` describing duplicate/null email issues before migration.\n- The preflight report must also mention dependent orders for dirty users `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`.\n- Also create `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/049-043-db-migration-safety-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-020905-9b40d74d/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql` that can restore the pre-migration schema shape with id, email, name, created_at.\n- The rollback script must be executable after the migration and must restore the old schema shape.\n- Also create `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/049-043-db-migration-safety-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-020905-9b40d74d/workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql` with verification queries that can be executed after the migration. It must check row counts, dependent order preservation, cleaned dirty-user emails, and email/status constraints.\n- Also create `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/049-043-db-migration-safety-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-020905-9b40d74d/workspace/in/db/migration_report.md` summarizing the migration strategy, dirty-data cleanup, idempotency approach, rollback limitation/behavior, and the postcheck queries to run.\n- The migration should run inside an explicit transaction and should be idempotent: running it a second time must not corrupt or duplicate user data.\n- Use deterministic cleanup values exactly: duplicate `u4` becomes `ada+u4@example.com`; null email `u5` becomes `missing+u5@example.invalid`; blank email `u6` becomes `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n\nThe migration must run offline in SQLite. Do not use external tools or services.\n"}],"timestamp":1788156553435},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning non-editable migration workflow**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a8b45bc87d2acb8ce80c3e90ae7\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning non-editable migration workflow**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_nxYFTc7oHIvS9D6h0wlS0Srt|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a8d25ec87d2b8dafd0353d78998","name":"todo","arguments":{"action":"create","title":"Make SQLite migration safe and add validation artifacts","body":"Read migration policy and schema; update migration.sql only among existing files, create preflight_report.md, rollback.sql, postcheck.sql, and migration_report.md. Validate offline SQLite behavior and idempotency."}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1593,"output":152,"cacheRead":12800,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":78,"totalTokens":14545,"cost":{"input":0.00031860000000000005,"output":0.0001824,"cacheRead":0.000256,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0007570000000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788156553443,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a8a898c87d29856640dcb66717f","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_nxYFTc7oHIvS9D6h0wlS0Srt|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a8d25ec87d2b8dafd0353d78998","toolName":"todo","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"TODO-57a23546\",\n  \"title\": \"Make SQLite migration safe and add validation artifacts\",\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"status\": \"open\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T06:09:18.092Z\",\n  \"body\": \"Read migration policy and schema; update migration.sql only among existing files, create preflight_report.md, rollback.sql, postcheck.sql, and migration_report.md. Validate offline SQLite behavior and idempotency.\"\n}"}],"details":{"action":"create","todo":{"id":"57a23546","title":"Make SQLite migration safe and add validation artifacts","tags":[],"status":"open","created_at":"2026-08-31T06:09:18.092Z","body":"Read migration policy and schema; update migration.sql only among existing files, create preflight_report.md, rollback.sql, postcheck.sql, and migration_report.md. Validate offline SQLite behavior and idempotency."}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788156558098},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Inspecting workflow list**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a8f0f6c87d291aeedccece9b979\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Inspecting workflow list**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Fxp8rabEb0SVDPvvVlhVi7be|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a8fba7087d2b0b582873d01efc0","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"list"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":839,"output":35,"cacheRead":13824,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":16,"totalTokens":14698,"cost":{"input":0.0001678,"output":0.000042,"cacheRead":0.00027648,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00048628}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788156558101,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a8e649c87d293157a218f9f0fac","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Fxp8rabEb0SVDPvvVlhVi7be|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a8fba7087d2b0b582873d01efc0","toolName":"workflow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"list\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"adversarial-verification\",\n      \"description\": \"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"task\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"verifier_count\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_repairs\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"accept_mean\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"reask_limit\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"classify-and-act\",\n      \"description\": \"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"categories\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"confidence_threshold\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"fan-out-and-synthesize\",\n      \"description\": \"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_branches\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"generate-and-filter\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_candidates\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"shortlist_size\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"use_judge\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"goal\",\n      \"description\": \"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"objective\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_turns\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"loop-until-done\",\n      \"description\": \"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_iterations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_scoring\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_repeats\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"open-claude-design\",\n      \"description\": \"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"discover_references\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ralph\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_loops\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tournament\",\n      \"description\": \"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_attempts\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"n_evaluations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"pivots\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"seed\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"models\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"action":"list","items":[{"name":"adversarial-verification","description":"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.","inputs":[{"name":"task","required":true},{"name":"verifier_count","required":false},{"name":"max_repairs","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"accept_mean","required":false},{"name":"reask_limit","required":false}]},{"name":"classify-and-act","description":"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"categories","required":false},{"name":"confidence_threshold","required":false}]},{"name":"fan-out-and-synthesize","description":"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_branches","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"generate-and-filter","description":"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_candidates","required":false},{"name":"shortlist_size","required":false},{"name":"use_judge","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"goal","description":"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"objective","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_turns","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"loop-until-done","description":"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_iterations","required":false},{"name":"progress_scoring","required":false},{"name":"progress_repeats","required":false}]},{"name":"open-claude-design","description":"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"discover_references","required":false}]},{"name":"ralph","description":"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_loops","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"tournament","description":"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_attempts","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false},{"name":"n_evaluations","required":false},{"name":"pivots","required":false},{"name":"seed","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"models","required":false}]}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788156560262},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning workflow launch with file validation**\n\n**Reviewing model pinning before launch**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a912f7087d2ab8c79189cf052bf\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning workflow launch with file validation**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Reviewing model pinning before launch**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Architecture: use one bounded `goal` run (implement → inspect policy/schema → validate SQLite migration/idempotency → report). The graph is acyclic; deterministic checks cover transaction, row/order counts, dirty-email cleanup, constraints, rollback shape, and second-run safety. The run will edit only the requested SQL migration and create the four requested artifacts; it will not touch `schema.sql` or `migration_policy.md`. Stop when checks pass, otherwise repair within the bounded run.\n\nStage | Model | Thinking | Role  \nImplement/review | workflow default | high | migration design and contract review  \nValidation | deterministic tools | — | SQLite execution and assertions  \nFinal report | workflow default | medium | concise evidence summary\n\nI’m launching the single tracked implementation run now.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a94489487d2bcb98368b7dce38a\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3brtcWvViVpRIEUzXha3tpMv|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a97019c87d2b7d1354851a5e398","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"run","workflow":"goal","inputs":{"objective":"<keepContext>Safely repair the SQLite migration task using the exact files and requirements in the user request. Read the migration_policy.md before editing. Work directly on the absolute target paths supplied by the user. Edit only migration.sql among existing files; do not modify schema.sql or migration_policy.md. Create preflight_report.md, rollback.sql, postcheck.sql, and migration_report.md as explicitly requested. Preserve all users, orders, user_id references, and historical created_at values. Add non-null status default active; enforce unique non-null emails for future writes; clean exactly u4 -> ada+u4@example.com, u5 -> missing+u5@example.invalid, u6 -> missing+u6@example.invalid. Use an explicit SQLite transaction and make migration reruns safe and non-corrupting. Validate offline by executing against a copy of the schema/data, run migration twice, run postchecks, and test rollback after migration. The rollback must restore users to old columns id,email,name,created_at while preserving data. Do not use external services.</keepContext>","acceptance_criteria":"<keepContext>All requested files exist at the exact absolute paths. migration.sql is policy-compliant, transactional, idempotent, preserves every user/order and order.user_id, retains created_at, adds status NOT NULL DEFAULT active, and enforces email uniqueness/non-null for future writes while deterministically cleaning the three dirty users. preflight_report.md documents duplicate/null/blank issues and explicitly mentions dependent orders for u4, u5, u6. rollback.sql executes after migration and restores old users schema shape with preserved data. postcheck.sql contains executable checks for row counts, dependent orders, cleaned emails, and email/status constraints. migration_report.md covers strategy, cleanup, idempotency, rollback behavior/limitation, and postcheck use. SQLite execution, second migration run, and rollback tests pass without edits to forbidden files.</keepContext>","max_turns":4},"budget":{"maxDurationMs":300000,"warnAtPercent":80}}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2321,"output":753,"cacheRead":13824,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":153,"totalTokens":16898,"cost":{"input":0.00046420000000000006,"output":0.0009036,"cacheRead":0.00027648,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00164428}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788156560263,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a90868c87d2b8690f0be591c0e0","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3brtcWvViVpRIEUzXha3tpMv|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951a97019c87d2b7d1354851a5e398","toolName":"workflow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"run\",\n  \"name\": \"goal\",\n  \"runId\": \"d7939cf9-cc2c-40d5-8a75-ecedb4821591\",\n  \"status\": \"blocked\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"status\": \"budget_exceeded\",\n    \"dimension\": \"duration\",\n    \"reading\": 726579,\n    \"ceiling\