provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":634,"output":174,"cacheRead":17920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":17,"totalTokens":18728,"cost":{"input":0.00012680000000000002,"output":0.00020879999999999998,"cacheRead":0.0003584,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000694}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788157325097,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d8d8e1887d29a79bb1b168177bc","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6f2NEvQOst2S492D0UXpCgYg|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d91bb1487d2aa1df5894ce04e4c","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/migration_policy.md#7D65]\n1:# Migration Policy\n2:\n3:The migration must preserve existing users and dependent order rows.\n4:\n5:Dirty email cleanup rules:\n6:- Keep the first existing `ada@example.com` row unchanged.\n7:- The duplicate user `u4` must become `ada+u4@example.com`.\n8:- The null email user `u5` must become `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n9:- The blank email user `u6` must become `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n10:- Future writes must reject duplicate or null emails.\n11:\n12:Schema rules:\n13:- Add `users.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n14:- Preserve historical `created_at`.\n15:- Preserve `orders.user_id` references to the same user ids.\n16:- The migration should run in an explicit transaction and be safe to run twice.\n17:\n18:Rollback:\n19:- `rollback.sql` must execute after the migration.\n20:- It must restore the pre-migration users schema shape: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n21:- It must preserve the same number of user rows and order rows, including dependent orders for dirty users."}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788157329888},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_U5OAxyL2Ndc4wNj089gHTues|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d91bb2487d2bd0e99769f910f13","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/schema.sql#14EF]\n1:PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n2:\n3:CREATE TABLE users (\n4:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n5:    email TEXT,\n6:    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n7:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n8:);\n9:\n10:INSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at) VALUES\n11:('u1', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada', '2024-01-02T10:00:00Z'),\n12:('u2', 'lin@example.com', 'Lin', '2024-02-03T11:30:00Z'),\n13:('u3', 'grace@example.com', 'Grace', '2024-03-04T09:15:00Z'),\n14:('u4', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada Legacy', '2023-12-01T08:00:00Z'),\n15:('u5', NULL, 'Null Email Legacy', '2023-11-05T12:00:00Z'),\n16:('u6', '', 'Blank Email Legacy', '2023-10-06T07:45:00Z');\n17:\n18:CREATE TABLE orders (\n19:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n20:    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n21:    total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n22:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n23:);\n24:\n25:INSERT INTO orders (id, user_id, total_cents, created_at) VALUES\n26:('o1', 'u1', 1299, '2024-04-01T09:00:00Z'),\n27:('o2', 'u4', 4599, '2024-04-02T10:30:00Z'),\n28:('o3', 'u5', 799, '2024-04-03T11:45:00Z'),\n29:('o4', 'u6', 1599, '2024-04-04T12:10:00Z');"}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/schema.sql","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/schema.sql"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788157329888},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6KxcAuakjnKJ2bLh6egvdC3z|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d91bb2c87d2849258ad661ef6c6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/migration.sql#BBC0]\n1:PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n2:\n3:BEGIN IMMEDIATE;\n4:\n5:CREATE TABLE users__new (\n6:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n7:    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n8:    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n9:    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n10:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n11:);\n12:\n13:INSERT INTO users__new (id, email, name, status, created_at)\n14:SELECT\n15:    id,\n16:    CASE id\n17:        WHEN 'u4' THEN 'ada+u4@example.com'\n18:        WHEN 'u5' THEN 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n19:        WHEN 'u6' THEN 'missing+u6@example.invalid'\n20:        ELSE email\n21:    END,\n22:    name,\n23:    'active',\n24:    created_at\n25:FROM users;\n26:\n27:DROP TABLE users;\n28:ALTER TABLE users__new RENAME TO users;\n29:\n30:COMMIT;\n31:\n32:PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;"}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788157329888},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ZTG8Pw9TlAX9LNGJ3kF5OauP|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d91bb3487d2bb37cf3f48124dcd","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md'"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1788157329888},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2KRRhIIVUVauxdeaiaydGzNg|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d91bb3c87d2a7108a1cd4a990ce","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql'"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1788157329888},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_pmj7xY01fj8xmU6DPBJTAkIU|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d91bb4487d28754c01209627d85","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql'"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1788157329888},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2ikKy1sIpg8jbLsnJLpKg4t5|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d91bb4c87d299422c31fe6e7d4b","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/workspace/in/db/migration_report.md'"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1788157329888},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Searching for external workflow references**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d9318fc87d2b79e5d5dee677957\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Searching for external workflow references**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_BL3Bw1sVVCKUoFuI00ArpyFX|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d93bbec87d2abf7dbad8d355fed","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"find /workspace -type f \\( -name preflight_report.md -o -name rollback.sql -o -name postcheck.sql -o -name migration_report.md \\) -print"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1870,"output":68,"cacheRead":17920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":11,"totalTokens":19858,"cost":{"input":0.00037400000000000004,"output":0.00008159999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0003584,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000814}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788157329890,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d92462887d2bfa653d7fce9f5df","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_BL3Bw1sVVCKUoFuI00ArpyFX|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d93bbec87d2abf7dbad8d355fed","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/workspace/out/preflight_report.md\n/workspace/out/postcheck.sql\n/workspace/out/migration_report.md\n/workspace/out/rollback.sql\n"}],"details":{"timeoutSeconds":300,"wallTimeMs":11},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788157332434},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Inspecting database migration workflow**\n\n**Designing idempotent migration with markers**\n\n**Planning transactional user table rebuild**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d95a64c87d2911cc6bd57d29138\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Inspecting database migration workflow**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing idempotent migration with markers**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning transactional user table rebuild**\"}]}"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning safe table renaming and recreation**\n\n**Designing idempotent user status migration**\n\n**Planning migration with idempotency marker**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d9f3f4c87d2aa4f188635d2e2e5\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning safe table renaming and recreation**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing idempotent user status migration**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning migration with idempotency marker**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_sKNqBXcOJJpT5trJWdjiEvv9|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951da8ae0887d2822c6c118e17905c","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql","content":"-- Transactional, rerunnable rebuild of users and orders.\n-- Dirty-data cleanup: retain the first ada@example.com row (u1), and assign\n-- deterministic unique values to u4, u5, and u6 before adding constraints.\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n\nBEGIN IMMEDIATE;\n\n-- Move both sides so the dependent rows are copied before either old table is removed.\nALTER TABLE users RENAME TO users__migration_old;\nALTER TABLE orders RENAME TO orders__migration_old;\n\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO users (id, email, name, status, created_at)\nSELECT\n    id,\n    CASE id\n        WHEN 'u4' THEN 'ada+u4@example.com'\n        WHEN 'u5' THEN 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n        WHEN 'u6' THEN 'missing+u6@example.invalid'\n        ELSE email\n    END,\n    name,\n    'active',\n    created_at\nFROM users__migration_old;\n\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n    total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO orders (id, user_id, total_cents, created_at)\nSELECT id, user_id, total_cents, created_at\nFROM orders__migration_old;\n\nDROP TABLE orders__migration_old;\nDROP TABLE users__migration_old;\n\nCOMMIT;\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":19899,"output":1421,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1030,"totalTokens":21320,"cost":{"input":0.0039798,"output":0.0017051999999999998,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.005685}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788157332436,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951d94d01887d299ea53e5e91977df","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_sKNqBXcOJJpT5trJWdjiEvv9|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951da8ae0887d2822c6c118e17905c","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/migration.sql#B0E9]\nSuccessfully wrote 1320 bytes to /workspace/in/db/migration.sql"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788157359345},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Designing migration with rollback and reporting**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_070ce35a7ebde320016a951db097f887d2a17e349041518fd2\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing migration with rollback and reporting**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_KKMmZ6YOVwgJDFn1qlMsXy7D|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951db3b35487d28a5febe0906954ab","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md","content":"# Preflight report\n\nThe source schema has 6 users and 4 orders.\n\nBefore migration, email data is dirty:\n\n- `u1` and `u4` both use `ada@example.com` (duplicate). Per policy, keep `u1` unchanged and migrate `u4` to `ada+u4@example.com`.\n- `u5.email` is `NULL`; migrate it to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n- `u6.email` is blank (`''`); migrate it to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n\nDependent orders must remain attached to the same user ids: dirty user `u4` has order `o2`, `u5` has `o3`, and `u6` has `o4`. The migration copies orders before removing the old users table, so these references remain intact.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2411,"output":344,"cacheRead":18944,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":130,"totalTokens":21699,"cost":{"input":0.00048220000000000007,"output":0.0004128,"cacheRead":0.00037888,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00127388}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788157359347,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951dafb60887d2ac0762bfce210a48","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_KKMmZ6YOVwgJDFn1qlMsXy7D|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951db3b35487d28a5febe0906954ab","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/preflight_report.md#99AE]\nSuccessfully wrote 604 bytes to /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788157366880},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_AFdSz220BGDVCfjhHE3T6X9J|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951db82fc087d280626cdf57acd02b","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql","content":"-- Restore the pre-migration users schema shape. Cleaned email values remain;\n-- original NULL/blank/duplicate values cannot be recovered from the migrated DB.\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n\nBEGIN IMMEDIATE;\n\nALTER TABLE users RENAME TO users__rollback_old;\nALTER TABLE orders RENAME TO orders__rollback_old;\n\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    email TEXT,\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at)\nSELECT id, email, name, created_at\nFROM users__rollback_old;\n\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n    total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO orders (id, user_id, total_cents, created_at)\nSELECT id, user_id, total_cents, created_at\nFROM orders__rollback_old;\n\nDROP TABLE orders__rollback_old;\nDROP TABLE users__rollback_old;\n\nCOMMIT;\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":741,"output":268,"cacheRead":20992,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":22001,"cost":{"input":0.00014820000000000002,"output":0.0003216,"cacheRead":0.00041984,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00088964}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788157366881,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951db7419087d2a340a9d27596c84a","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_AFdSz220BGDVCfjhHE3T6X9J|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951db82fc087d280626cdf57acd02b","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/rollback.sql#269C]\nSuccessfully wrote 901 bytes to /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788157372997},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xcrXINO0NB7AM7Rh0ij1Vv8Y|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951dbe50c487d2a0cc0d009ac04f1e","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql","content":"-- Each result should be 0 (no violation), except the two count queries which\n-- should each return 6 and 4 respectively.\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS user_count FROM users;\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS order_count FROM orders;\n\n-- No order was lost or retargeted; these are the expected dirty-user links.\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS missing_dirty_user_orders\nFROM (SELECT 'u4' AS user_id, 'o2' AS order_id\n      UNION ALL SELECT 'u5', 'o3'\n      UNION ALL SELECT 'u6', 'o4') expected\nWHERE NOT EXISTS (\n    SELECT 1 FROM orders o\n    WHERE o.id = expected.order_id AND o.user_id = expected.user_id\n);\n\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS cleaned_email_violations\nFROM (SELECT 'u4' AS id, 'ada+u4@example.com' AS email\n      UNION ALL SELECT 'u5', 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n      UNION ALL SELECT 'u6', 'missing+u6@example.invalid') expected\nJOIN users u ON u.id = expected.id\nWHERE u.email <> expected.email;\n\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS null_email_violations FROM users WHERE email IS NULL;\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS blank_email_violations FROM users WHERE trim(email) = '';\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS duplicate_email_violations\nFROM users a JOIN users b ON a.email = b.email AND a.id < b.id;\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS null_status_violations FROM users WHERE status IS NULL;\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS inactive_default_violations FROM users WHERE status <> 'active';\n\n-- Constraint probes: each INSERT must fail with a NOT NULL or UNIQUE error.\n-- Run these manually in a transaction and ROLLBACK afterward:\n-- INSERT INTO users(id,email,name,created_at) VALUES ('__postcheck_null__',NULL,'x','x');\n-- INSERT INTO users(id,email,name,created_at) VALUES ('__postcheck_dup__','ada@example.com','x','x');\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1041,"output":460,"cacheRead":20992,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":22493,"cost":{"input":0.00020820000000000002,"output":0.000552,"cacheRead":0.00041984,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0011800399999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788157372999,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951dbd582887d29c2ef9683e241cde","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_xcrXINO0NB7AM7Rh0ij1Vv8Y|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951dbe50c487d2a0cc0d009ac04f1e","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/postcheck.sql#828F]\nSuccessfully wrote 1622 bytes to /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788157382542},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_pvfEZirntnACOM9VFmztYrdq|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951dc7b67087d2a37ca1e2daf28df5","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","content":"# Migration report\n\n## Strategy\n\n`migration.sql` runs in one explicit `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction. It renames both `users` and its dependent `orders`, creates the constrained users table, copies users, creates orders with its foreign key, copies every order, then drops the old tables and commits. Historical `created_at`, user ids, order ids, totals, and `orders.user_id` values are copied unchanged.\n\n## Dirty-data cleanup\n\nThe first `ada@example.com` row (`u1`) stays unchanged. The duplicate `u4` becomes `ada+u4@example.com`; null `u5` becomes `missing+u5@example.invalid`; blank `u6` becomes `missing+u6@example.invalid`. The new users table declares `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` and `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n\n## Idempotency\n\nA second run repeats the rebuild against the already-clean users and orders tables. The same ids are copied once into newly created tables, with no append or duplicate operation, and the deterministic cleanup values remain unchanged. The whole operation rolls back on any failure.\n\n## Rollback behavior and limitation\n\n`rollback.sql` uses the same dependent-table copy order and restores users to `id, email, name, created_at`, while retaining all users and orders. It cannot reconstruct the original dirty email values after migration because cleanup is lossy; it retains the migrated deterministic values. Status is intentionally removed.\n\n## Postcheck\n\nRun `postcheck.sql` after migration. The first two queries must return 6 users and 4 orders. All subsequent count queries must return 0. The listed constraint probes should fail with NOT NULL and UNIQUE errors (run each in a transaction and roll it back).\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":22526,"output":397,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":22923,"cost":{"input":0.0045052,"output":0.0004764,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0049816}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788157382543,"responseId":"resp_070ce35a7ebde320016a951dc6d7d087d2a077f95455df848c","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_pvfEZirntnACOM9VFmztYrdq|fc_070ce35a7ebde320016a951dc7b67087